{"word": "notebook", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "notebook", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈnəʊtˌbʊk/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈnoʊtˌbʊk/", "tags": ["General American"]}], "forms": [{"word": "notebooks", "tags": ["plural"]}, {"word": "note book", "tags": ["alternative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "A book (physical or digital) in which notes or memoranda are written.", "tags": [], "examples": ["Near-synonyms: notepad, rough book, writing pad, logbook, journal"], "quotes": [{"text": "For Caſſius is a-weary of the World: / Hated by one he loues, brau'd by his Brother, / Check'd like a bondman, all his faults obſeru'd, / Set in a Note-booke, learn'd, and con'd by roate / To caſt into my Teeth.", "reference": "1599 (first performance), William Shakespeare, “The Tragedie of Iulius Cæsar”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act IV, scene iii], page 125, column 1:"}, {"text": "With an unquenchable enthusiasm for locomotives and their work, at an early age I had commenced to keep engine and traffic-recording notebooks, compiled in a schoolboy's round hand.", "reference": "1946 March and April, R. A. H. Weight, “Euston to the North-West”, in Railway Magazine, page 69:"}], "synonyms": ["by-book", "notepad", "rough book", "writing pad", "logbook", "journal"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(computing, sometimes attributive) A kind of user interface in literate programming, allowing calculations to be interspersed with human-readable comments, diagrams, etc.", "tags": ["attributive", "sometimes"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "We have found the use of Jupyter notebooks to be a convenient way of sharing work and code in a compact and reproducible manner. Jupyter notebooks are easy to update and adapt over time compared to a static CD-ROM.", "reference": "2016, David Ming, David Glasser, Diane Hildebrandt, Attainable Region Theory, page 317:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(computing) Ellipsis of notebook computer (“laptop computer”).", "tags": ["abbreviation", "alt of", "ellipsis"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Over time, the difference in size between laptops and notebooks became a matter of no more than an inch or two in length and width, and a fraction of an inch in thickness.", "reference": "2006, Corey Sandler, Upgrading and Fixing Laptops For Dummies, page 8:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "كَمْبْيُوتَر مَحْمُول"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "حَاسُوب مَحْمُول"}, {"language": {"code": "arz", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "لاب توب"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "նոթբուք"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "նոութբուք"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "noutbuk"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "но́ўтбук"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "лэпто́п"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "но́утбук"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "筆記本 /笔记本"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "手提計算機 /手提计算机"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "筆記本電腦 /笔记本电脑"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "notebook"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "notlibra komputilo"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "tekokomputilo"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "sülearvuti"}, {"language": {"code": "fo", "name": "Faroese"}, "word": "fartelda"}, {"la